{"blocks":[["beehiv/","source-block-1249","Podcast workflow:",["beehiv (Beehiiv)","Comparison with substack"]],["beehiv/","source-block-1271","Beehiiv: supports podcast website pages and RSS-driven sync for episodes.",["beehiv (Beehiiv)","Comparison with substack","Podcast workflow:"]],["beehiv/","source-block-1350","Substack: supports creating/importing podcasts and distributing to major podcast apps.",["beehiv (Beehiiv)","Comparison with substack","Podcast workflow:"]],["beehiv/","source-block-1442","Practical takeaway:",["beehiv (Beehiiv)","Comparison with substack"]],["beehiv/","source-block-1466","Beehiiv often fits creators optimizing for configurable monetization and owned-site workflows.",["beehiv (Beehiiv)","Comparison with substack","Practical takeaway:"]],["beehiv/","source-block-1566","Substack often fits creators optimizing for in-network discovery and reader graph effects.",["beehiv (Beehiiv)","Comparison with substack","Practical takeaway:"]],["beehiv/","source-block-1662","Sources",["beehiv (Beehiiv)"]],["beehiv/","source-block-1676","Beehiiv homepage: https://www.beehiiv.com/",["beehiv (Beehiiv)","Sources"]],["beehiv/","source-block-1723","Beehiiv podcast feature page: https://www.beehiiv.com/features/podcasts",["beehiv (Beehiiv)","Sources"]],["beehiv/","source-block-1799","Beehiiv paid subscriptions feature page: https://www.beehiiv.com/features/paid-subscriptions",["beehiv (Beehiiv)","Sources"]],["beehiv/","source-block-1896","Beehiiv Ad Network FAQ: https://www.beehiiv.com/support/article/17507491038231",["beehiv (Beehiiv)","Sources"]],["beehiv/","source-block-1979","Substack pricing/fees: https://support.substack.com/hc/en-us/articles/360037607131-How-much-does-Substack-cost",["beehiv (Beehiiv)","Sources"]],["beehiv/","source-block-2094","Substack recommendations: https://support.substack.com/hc/en-us/articles/5036794583828-How-can-I-recommend-other-publications-on-Substack",["beehiv (Beehiiv)","Sources"]],["beehiv/","source-block-2236","Substack podcast publishing: https://support.substack.com/hc/en-us/articles/360037462092-How-do-I-create-and-publish-a-podcast-on-Substack",["beehiv (Beehiiv)","Sources"]],["behave/","source-block-129","behave",[]],["behave/","source-block-205","A Python Behavior/Driven/Development framework that runs feature specifications against step definitions written in Python.",["behave"]],["behave/","source-block-336","Standard project layout centers on a features/ directory containing .feature files written in Gherkin plus Python step implementations.",["behave"]],["behave/Docs/","source-block-0","behave 1.4.0.dev0 documentation",[]],["Behavior/Driven/Development/","source-block-17","Behavior Driven Development (BDD)",[]],["Behavior/Driven/Development/","source-block-55","A method of writing Software that usually entails describing the Requirements ahead of time.",["Behavior Driven Development (BDD)"]],["Behavior/Driven/Development/","source-block-159","One framework for using BDD is the Py/Lib behave, which uses a modified form of Gherkin, which is the DSL for BDD originally written for Cucumber, a cross-language BDD framework.",["Behavior Driven Development (BDD)"]],["Behavior/Driven/Development/","source-block-361","Examples of a software projects using BDD",["Behavior Driven Development (BDD)"]],["Behavior/Driven/Development/","source-block-410","tk",["Behavior Driven Development (BDD)","Examples of a software projects using BDD"]],["Behavior/Expected/","source-block-47","Expected Behavior",[]],["Behavior/Expected/","source-block-69","the behavior one expects, usually of a system",["Expected Behavior"]],["Behavior/Observed/","source-block-47","Observed Behavior",[]],["Behavior/Observed/","source-block-69","a behavior that has been observed of an entity or an application",["Observed Behavior"]],["Behavior/Observed/","source-block-137","in the case of a Bug, the observed behavior contradicts the Expected Behavior",["Observed Behavior","a behavior that has been observed of an entity or an application"]],["Bellingcat/","source-block-0","bellingcat - the home of online investigations",[]],["Bellingcat/Investigation%20Toolkit/","source-block-20","About | Bellingcat's Online Investigation Toolkit",[]],["BenjiLifeOS/","source-block-21","Benji - The Life OS",[]],["BetterStack/","source-block-0","Better Stack - Observability Meets Incident Management",[]],["Bevy/","source-block-0","Bevy",[]],["Bevy/","source-block-27","Rust Video Game Engine",["Bevy"]],["Bevy/","source-block-61","Examples",["Bevy"]],["Bevy/","source-block-76","Game/Video/CLRS — minimal RTS / territory control game",["Bevy","Examples"]],["Bevy/","source-block-141","Game/Video/Gaia Maker - planet and terraforming simulation game",["Bevy","Examples"]],["Bevy/","source-block-213","Game/Video/Pico TD — pixel-art tower defense game",["Bevy","Examples"]],["Bevy/","source-block-273","Game/Video/Enty TD — mining tower defense game",["Bevy","Examples"]],["Bevy/","source-block-330","Top games for Web made with Bevy Engine - itch.io",["Bevy","Examples"]],["Bevy/","source-block-444","lots and lots of examples",["Bevy","Examples","Top games for Web made with Bevy Engine - itch.io"]],["Bibio/","source-block-92","Bibio",[]],["Bibio/","source-block-133","Recording identity of British producer, songwriter and multi-instrumentalist Person/Stephen Wilkinson.",["Bibio"]],["Bibio/Music/Recording/Answers/","source-block-366","Answers",[]],["Bibio/Music/Recording/Answers/","source-block-406","Debut collaborative album by Bibio and Dorian Concept. Released on 16 October 2026; Bandcamp release and credits.",["Answers"]],["Bibio/Music/Recording/Answers/","source-block-575","Collaboration",["Answers"]],["Bibio/Music/Recording/Answers/","source-block-595","Built through experimentation and improvisation, combining traditional instruments with layered electronic textures. Warp describes the album as looking to the past to develop new music.",["Answers","Collaboration"]],["Bibio/Music/Recording/Answers/","source-block-786","The collaboration follows Bibio’s appearance on An Unopened Letter, the closing track of Dorian Concept/Music/Recording/Miniatures.",["Answers","Collaboration"]],["Bibio/Music/Recording/Answers/","source-block-928","The release page includes official videos for Womb Glow, Hammock Portal, Lichen Trip and Shame.",["Answers","Collaboration"]],["Bibio/Music/Recording/Answers/","source-block-1028","My Notes",["Answers"]],["Bibio/Music/Recording/Answers/","source-block-1051","Tracks",["Answers"]],["Bibio/Music/Recording/Answers/","source-block-1064","01 - Womb Glow",["Answers","Tracks"]],["Bibio/Music/Recording/Answers/","source-block-1083","02 - Lichen Trip",["Answers","Tracks"]],["Bibio/Music/Recording/Answers/","source-block-1104","03 - Shame",["Answers","Tracks"]],["Bibio/Music/Recording/Answers/","source-block-1119","04 - Pigeon Harp",["Answers","Tracks"]],["Bibio/Music/Recording/Answers/","source-block-1140","05 - Hammock Portal",["Answers","Tracks"]],["Bibio/Music/Recording/Answers/","source-block-1168","My Notes",["Answers","Tracks","05 - Hammock Portal"]],["Bibio/Music/Recording/Answers/","source-block-1186","I like the Music/Video to Hammock Portal, which features a rotating view of a tree canopy in the beginning. About a minute in, a major whoosh enters, and a slow pulse (possibly sub 30 BPM) ensues. The concept of the video changes to phases of blasted-out, blurred CRT and RGB scenes, infra-red-ish videography, with some masking and layering.",["Tracks","05 - Hammock Portal","My Notes"]],["Bibio/Music/Recording/Answers/","source-block-1545","06 - Jelly Pencil",["Answers","Tracks"]],["Bibio/Music/Recording/Answers/","source-block-1567","07 - Pearl Net",["Answers","Tracks"]],["Bibio/Music/Recording/Answers/","source-block-1590","My Notes",["Answers","Tracks","07 - Pearl Net"]],["Bibio/Music/Recording/Answers/","source-block-1608","A brief piece, but the Music/Video has a cool valence; whooshing water, glistening.",["Tracks","07 - Pearl Net","My Notes"]],["Bibio/Music/Recording/Answers/","source-block-1702","08 - Pins & Needles",["Answers","Tracks"]],["Bibio/Music/Recording/Answers/","source-block-1730","My Notes",["Answers","Tracks","08 - Pins & Needles"]],["Bibio/Music/Recording/Answers/","source-block-1748","Begins with some ASMR effects. Close mic breathing.",["Tracks","08 - Pins & Needles","My Notes"]],["Bibio/Music/Recording/Answers/","source-block-1810","09 - Sugar Rain",["Answers","Tracks"]],["Bibio/Music/Recording/Answers/","source-block-1830","10 - The Unknown",["Answers","Tracks"]],["Bibio/Music/Recording/Answers/","source-block-1851","11 - Star Bird",["Answers","Tracks"]],["Bibio/Music/Recording/Answers/","source-block-1870","12 - Stratocumulus",["Answers","Tracks"]],["Bibio/Music/Recording/Answers/","source-block-1893","13 - Pomegranate",["Answers","Tracks"]],["Bibio/Music/Recording/Fi/","source-block-301","Fi",[]],["Bibio/Music/Recording/Fi/","source-block-347","Bibio’s debut album, originally released by Mush Records in 2005. Warp reissued it on 27 November 2015. Original release history. The track list below follows the Warp reissue, whose closing track is the uncut version of Poplar Avenue.",["Fi"]],["Bibio/Music/Recording/Fi/","source-block-632","Tracks",["Fi"]],["Bibio/Music/Recording/Fi/","source-block-645","01 - Cherry Blossom Road",["Fi","Tracks"]],["Bibio/Music/Recording/Fi/","source-block-674","02 - Bewley In White",["Fi","Tracks"]],["Bibio/Music/Recording/Fi/","source-block-699","03 - Puffer",["Fi","Tracks"]],["Bibio/Music/Recording/Fi/","source-block-715","04 - Cluster At Cwm Einion",["Fi","Tracks"]],["Bibio/Music/Recording/Fi/","source-block-746","05 - London Planes",["Fi","Tracks"]],["Bibio/Music/Recording/Fi/","source-block-769","06 - It Was Willow",["Fi","Tracks"]],["Bibio/Music/Recording/Fi/","source-block-792","07 - I’m Rewinding It…",["Fi","Tracks"]],["Bibio/Music/Recording/Fi/","source-block-823","08 - Looking Through The Facets Of A Plastic Jewel",["Fi","Tracks"]],["Bibio/Mus